WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.767
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.734
Yeah, enjoy yourself. Welcome.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:06.834
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.634
Well, this is fun --
over the weekend,

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.133
the Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.934
arrived in New York City.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.133
This is real. Can we see it?

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.868
Hm.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:25.834
-The what?

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:28.167
-They never look as good as
they do in their dating profile.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.934
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.434
Don't worry.
They're trying to turn the tree

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.501
so the giant gap faces the wall.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.834
Do you know what I'm saying?
Let's get to some news.

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.100
On Saturday, former president
Trump's youngest daughter,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.701
Tiffany,
got married at Mar-a-Lago.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.033
Yeah, the cutest part
of the wedding

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.033
was when Eric Trump
carried the ring down the aisle

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.334
on a tiny pillow.
It was very cute.

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:49.300
And there was a special moment
when Trump was like,

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.834
"Well, if I'm giving kids away,
will someone take Don Jr.?"

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.968
Of course, everyone was talking
about the reception

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.567
when Tiffany threw the bouquet

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.400
and Melania elbowed
six other women to catch it.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.634
And you go,
"Wait a minute. No."

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:04.367
The only issue at the wedding --

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.000
they were supposed to have
a ton of seats,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.868
but somehow Trump lost them all.

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.467
-Ohh! Oh!

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:13.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.567
[ Applause ]

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.834
-Yep, Tiffany Trump
got married at Mar-a-Lago,

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:20.501
and I don't know how this
happened, but we got our hands

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.033
on a recording of Trump's
"father of the bride" speech.

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.467
-Wow.
-Yeah, listen to this.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.067
[Jimmy as Pres. Trump] Forgive
me. I'm gonna read my toast.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.601
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:14.300
Aww. That was so sweet.
That's so nice.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.934
[ Applause ]

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:20.767
Switching gears, President Biden
just arrived in Bali

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.267
for the G20 summit.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.968
And when he landed, he received
an extra-special greeting.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.200
Take a look at this.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:33.033
♪♪

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:36.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.467
-I can't tell whether Biden's
happy, confused, or both.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:42.767
He's like...

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:49.234
Meanwhile, today in Bali,
Biden held his first

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:52.067
in-person meeting
with Chinese President Xi

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:55.000
since taking office,
and it lasted three hours.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.000
For both men, the hardest part
was pretending that they didn't

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.234
hack the other person's e-mails
to see what they'd say.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:00.734
Yeah.

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.133
That's right.
Biden and Xi met in person

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.067
for the first time
since Biden took office,

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:06.467
and their first handshake
was captured in a video.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:07.868
Check this out.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:12.601
[ Young-Holt Unlimited's
"Soulful Strut" plays ]

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:19.934
♪♪

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:22.400
Wow. Amazing moment.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.834
That's -- Wow.
-Wow!

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.701
-I think it went well.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.968
Some more big political news.
Over the weekend,

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:30.934
Democrats learned that they'd
won control of the Senate.

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:33.100
Yep. For breaking news...

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:36.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.501
For the breaking-news alert,
MSNBC played...

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.801
[ Rasta horn blares ]

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.300
While Fox News played...

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.834
[ Sad trombone plays ]

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.100
Yeah.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.000
Democrats are giving credit
to Gen Z,

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.834
who really showed up to vote.

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.267
Republicans were like, "How did
Gen Z vote for Democrats?

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:55.067
All we were trying to do was
stop student-loan forgiveness."

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.067
In other political news,
I saw that Mark Kelly

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.367
defeated Blake Masters
in Arizona.

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.801
But --
-I did -- I did what?

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.801
-What?
-Did you say my name?

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.334
-I'm sorry, Mark. I was talking
about Mark Kelly, the Senator,

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:07.834
not Mark Kelley from The Roots.

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:09.467
You have the same name.

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.400
-Oh, my bad.
This happens a lot.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.067
People get us mixed up
constantly.

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.767
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:18.267
I'll show you what I mean
in a new segment called

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.267
"Mark Kelly or Mark Kelley?"

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.067
-♪ Is it Mark Kelly
or Mark Kelley? ♪

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:24.033
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.334
-You guys wrote
an intro song for this?

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:28.234
-Okay, let's take a look
at the differences

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:31.067
between Mark Kelly
and me, Mark Kelley.

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:34.234
First up, Mark Kelly
is an astronaut.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:37.834
Meanwhile, Mark Kelley
is a sick-ass bassist.

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:41.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.834
-When did you make all --

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:44.334
When did you make
all these graphics?

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:46.701
-Up next,
Mark Kelly has a twin brother.

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:50.400
Meanwhile, Mark Kelley
is a sick-ass bassist.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:54.100
-Please stop saying "sick-ass."

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.200
-Jimmy, stop interrupting me!
It's very rude!

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.601
-You interrupted me.
-It's my time to shine.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.300
Everyone's been talking
about this cool,

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.868
bald astronaut senator
with my name,

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:07.267
and I'm tired of it.

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:08.868
I've always been
the cool Mark Kelley,

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:11.634
and now this dude comes along
and steals my thunder.

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:15.000
I'm hurt. And I'm scared.
And I'd appreciate it

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.033
if you'd let me have this
one tiny thing, okay?!

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.367
-Geez, I'm sorry, Mark.

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:21.367
I didn't realize you were
so upset about it. Go ahead.

00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:24.567
-Thank you. Up next,
Mark Kelly lives in Arizona.

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:27.033
While Mark Kelley
is a sick-ass bassist.

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.400
-Alright. Come on.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.434
You can't just keep saying that.

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:32.767
-You know what?
-What?

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:35.067
-I don't have to put up
with this. I'm out of here.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.601
Who's with me?!

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:42.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:50.334
-Who's with him?

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:52.234
Who's with him?
The real Mark Kelley, everybody.

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:53.467
He'll come back.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.934
"Who's with me?"

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:00.968
This is going viral --
On Friday night,

00:06:00.968 --> 00:06:02.567
during a live
college basketball game,

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.133
