00:12:01.033 --> 00:12:02.367
Check this out.

00:12:02.367 --> 00:12:04.667
-If the thought of running
a marathon has you winded,

00:12:04.667 --> 00:12:07.968
imagine doing it while smoking
a pack of cigs.

00:12:07.968 --> 00:12:12.901
He completed all 26.2 miles in
3 hours and 28 minutes.

00:12:12.901 --> 00:12:15.634
-Wow! This guy's a legend.

00:12:15.634 --> 00:12:19.234
He's already on the front of
the box of Wheezies.

00:12:20.701 --> 00:12:21.868
I don't know
if you guys saw this,

00:12:21.868 --> 00:12:24.634
but for the last 24 hours,
#RIPJimmyFallon

00:12:24.634 --> 00:12:26.767
has been trending on Twitter.

00:12:26.767 --> 00:12:29.133
Yeah. Even worse,
when they heard I died,

00:12:29.133 --> 00:12:31.767
Ticketmaster kicked me out of
line for Taylor Swift tickets.

00:12:31.767 --> 00:12:35.400
And I go, "This is terrible.
This is awful."

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.834
Right after it happened, though,
I was so touched that NBC

00:12:37.834 --> 00:12:39.934
immediately called and asked,

00:12:39.934 --> 00:12:41.834
"How can we turn this into
another 'Law &amp; Order'?"

00:12:41.834 --> 00:12:43.667
And I go, "What?"

00:12:43.667 --> 00:12:47.567
Yeah, #RIPJimmyFallon was
the number-2 trend on Twitter.

00:12:47.567 --> 00:12:49.334
I tried everything I could
to bump it down.

00:12:49.334 --> 00:12:51.701
I even tried the hashtag
#RIPPEDJimmyFallon

00:12:51.701 --> 00:12:53.267
I thought that would maybe help.

00:12:53.267 --> 00:12:54.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.200
Let's get to
the number-1 trending topic.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:57.367
Everyone's talking about this.

00:12:57.367 --> 00:12:58.667
Last night,
former president Trump

00:12:58.667 --> 00:13:02.501
announced that he's running
for president in 2024.

00:13:02.501 --> 00:13:04.601
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:13:04.601 --> 00:13:05.934
When I heard Trump
was running again,

00:13:05.934 --> 00:13:07.467
I said, "Over my dead body."

00:13:07.467 --> 00:13:09.501
Yeah.

00:13:09.501 --> 00:13:12.634
-Hey-oh!
♪♪

00:13:12.634 --> 00:13:14.801
-That's right -- Trump's
running for a third time.

00:13:14.801 --> 00:13:17.367
Here he is making the
announcement from Mar-a-Lago.

00:13:17.367 --> 00:13:20.033
-In order to make America
great and glorious again,

00:13:20.033 --> 00:13:22.868
I am tonight announcing
my candidacy for

00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:24.934
President of the United States.

00:13:24.934 --> 00:13:26.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:26.801 --> 00:13:32.267
-I know we are, but why does he
seem like he's already over it?

00:13:32.267 --> 00:13:33.601
What a moment.

00:13:33.601 --> 00:13:37.567
You can really feel the
indictment -- I mean excitement.

00:13:37.567 --> 00:13:41.067
Yep, Trump wants to make America
"great and glorious again,"

00:13:41.067 --> 00:13:43.734
or as it will now be known,
MAGAGA.

00:13:46.868 --> 00:13:49.801
[ As Trump ] Lady MAGAGA.

00:13:49.801 --> 00:13:53.234
Itchy gichy ya MAGAGA.

00:13:53.234 --> 00:13:54.934
[ Normal voice ] As always,
Trump covered a lot of ground

00:13:54.934 --> 00:13:56.167
during his speech,
and he even gave

00:13:56.167 --> 00:13:57.300
a shout-out to his son Eric.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.434
Watch this.

00:13:58.434 --> 00:14:00.501
-My one boy -- Stand up, Eric.

00:14:00.501 --> 00:14:01.901
I think he got more subpoenas

00:14:01.901 --> 00:14:04.534
than any man in
the history of our country.

00:14:04.534 --> 00:14:06.534
So unfair.

00:14:06.534 --> 00:14:07.601
Al Capone.

00:14:07.601 --> 00:14:09.634
You all heard
of the great gangster?

00:14:09.634 --> 00:14:11.868
Al Capone got far less.

00:14:11.868 --> 00:14:13.534
Eric Trump got more subpoenas.

00:14:13.534 --> 00:14:15.968
He's a PhD in subpoenas.

00:14:15.968 --> 00:14:19.200
And I appreciate the job you do
and the abuse that you've taken.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:22.334
-Whoa.

00:14:22.334 --> 00:14:24.334
-It's ironic,
because at Trump University,

00:14:24.334 --> 00:14:27.767
you can actually get a PhD
in subpoenas.

00:14:27.767 --> 00:14:28.901
He's like, "That's Eric.

00:14:28.901 --> 00:14:32.534
He's got that
big subpoenas energy."

00:14:35.801 --> 00:14:38.400
Yeah, but Trump was advised
to speak for only 45 minutes,

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.467
but he went on for over an hour.

00:14:40.467 --> 00:14:41.968
In fact, Trump rambled on
for so long

00:14:41.968 --> 00:14:45.734
that even Fox News
cut away from the speech.

00:14:45.734 --> 00:14:46.834
That's real.

00:14:46.834 --> 00:14:48.300
The relationship
has gotten so bad,

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.701
"Fox &amp; Friends" now say they're
just "Fox &amp; Acquaintances."

00:14:50.701 --> 00:14:52.501
Some more political news.

00:14:52.501 --> 00:14:54.367
Today, Senator Mitch McConnell
was re-elected

00:14:54.367 --> 00:14:55.734
as Senate minority leader,

00:14:55.734 --> 00:14:58.334
beating Florida Senator
Rick Scott.

00:14:58.334 --> 00:14:59.868
Can we see McConnell and Scott?

00:14:59.868 --> 00:15:06.334
Yeah, it's the first time the
tortoise has beat the no-hair.

00:15:06.334 --> 00:15:08.334
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:15:10.667 --> 00:15:12.601
Well, switching gears,
as I mentioned earlier,

00:15:12.601 --> 00:15:14.801
Taylor Swift tickets
went on presale yesterday,

00:15:14.801 --> 00:15:18.634
and there was such high demand
that Ticketmaster crashed.

00:15:18.634 --> 00:15:20.133
Everyone was
furious at Ticketmaster,

00:15:20.133 --> 00:15:21.901
so they posted
this message basically just

00:15:21.901 --> 00:15:24.367
telling people to be patient.

00:15:24.367 --> 00:15:25.934
Be patient.

00:15:25.934 --> 00:15:27.167
Obviously,
that didn't go over well.

00:15:27.167 --> 00:15:29.300
So then Ticketmaster
posted more updates.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.400
First, there's...

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.200
That's not going to help.
Then there was...

00:15:40.467 --> 00:15:41.567
Then they said...

00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:47.234
Yeah. Then they said...

00:15:49.667 --> 00:15:50.834
And finally...

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:56.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:56.868 --> 00:15:58.601
That's not helpful.

00:16:00.567 --> 00:16:01.934
Hey, get this.

00:16:01.934 --> 00:16:05.167
In response to Costco's
$1.50 hot-dog-and-drink combo,

00:16:05.167 --> 00:16:09.300
Sam's Club is now offering
the same meal for $1.38.

00:16:10.634 --> 00:16:12.501
Meanwhile, 7-Eleven is like,
"If you're brave enough

00:16:12.501 --> 00:16:15.133
to eat our hot dogs,
we'll pay you $1.50."

00:16:15.133 --> 00:16:17.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:19.634 --> 00:16:21.801
And, finally,
according to UN estimates,

00:16:21.801 --> 00:16:24.834
the world population reached
8 billion people this week.

00:16:24.834 --> 00:16:26.000
That's a huge milestone.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.667
The UN actually released
all sorts of data

00:16:27.667 --> 00:16:29.968
about the population, and it's
pretty interesting to see.

00:16:29.968 --> 00:16:31.133
Let's take a look.

00:16:31.133 --> 00:16:33.501
When it comes to the global
population...

00:16:40.267 --> 00:16:42.267
[ Applause ]

00:16:46.133 --> 00:16:47.334
Check out some more data here.

00:16:56.167 --> 00:16:58.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:58.734 --> 00:16:59.868
Here's another one.

00:17:06.801 --> 00:17:09.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.534
I'm 6'7".
Next up...

00:17:17.901 --> 00:17:22.000
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.167
And, finally...

00:17:30.033 --> 00:17:31.968
Well, guys,
it is the holiday season,

00:17:31.968 --> 00:17:34.734
but, apparently, not everyone
is feeling so festive.

00:17:34.734 --> 00:17:36.934
CNN just announced
that they're no longer

00:17:36.934 --> 00:17:39.834
allowing their anchors to drink,
on- or off-camera,

00:17:39.834 --> 00:17:42.534
during the network's
New Year's Eve coverage.

00:17:42.534 --> 00:17:44.067
[ Booing ]
-Come on.

00:17:44.067 --> 00:17:46.234
-When they heard that,
Andy Cohen and Anderson Cooper

00:17:46.234 --> 00:17:48.000
were like,
"Okay, edibles, it is.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.901
[ Laughter and applause ]
That's it. You said it."

00:17:49.901 --> 00:17:51.367
-Yes!

00:17:51.367 --> 00:17:53.868
-That's right,
no drinking on New Year's Eve.

00:17:53.868 --> 00:17:55.133
At that point, it's not a party.

00:17:55.133 --> 00:17:57.033
It's just a news channel
filming a clock.

00:17:57.033 --> 00:17:58.501
[ Laughter ]
Do you know what I'm saying?

00:17:58.501 --> 00:18:00.667
Seriously, why would CNN mess
with the one night

00:18:00.667 --> 00:18:02.300
people actually watch CNN?

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:04.067
I don't know why they --
[ Laughter ]

00:18:04.067 --> 00:18:06.300
Speaking of CNN, last night,
they hosted a town hall

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.801
with former vice president
Mike Pence.

00:18:08.801 --> 00:18:10.767
And, ironically,
it had all the excitement

00:18:10.767 --> 00:18:12.334
of a sober New Year's Eve party.

00:18:12.334 --> 00:18:13.767
[ Laughter ]

00:18:13.767 --> 00:18:16.968
Yep, no drinking on New Year's
and a Mike Pence town hall.

00:18:16.968 --> 00:18:18.901
It explains why they just
changed their slogan to...

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:22.868
[ Laughter ]

00:18:22.868 --> 00:18:25.267
CNN hosted a town hall
with the former vice president,

00:18:25.267 --> 00:18:26.868
and I noticed that Pence
has some trouble

00:18:26.868 --> 00:18:28.033
remembering everyone's name.

00:18:28.033 --> 00:18:29.334
Take a look at this.
Watch this.

00:18:29.334 --> 00:18:32.734
-Meet Andrea Barber-Dansby
from Anderson, Indiana.

00:18:32.734 --> 00:18:33.767
-Andrea.
-Hi, Barbara.

00:18:33.767 --> 00:18:36.100
-Hello.
-Barbara, thank you.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:39.868
I represented Madison County
in Congress for many years.

00:18:39.868 --> 00:18:40.968
-Andrea.

00:18:40.968 --> 00:18:42.634
[ Laughter ]
-It's nice to see you.

00:18:42.634 --> 00:18:44.033
-Daniela Moloci.

00:18:44.033 --> 00:18:45.267
She's from Fort Wayne.

00:18:45.267 --> 00:18:48.033
-Oh, Michele, uh,
good to have you here.

00:18:49.601 --> 00:18:50.701
-And --
-Daniela, Daniela.

00:18:50.701 --> 00:18:52.167
-Danielle, forgive me.

00:18:52.167 --> 00:18:53.834
We have a process
in this country

00:18:53.834 --> 00:18:57.067
where states conduct
elections, Jack.

00:18:57.067 --> 00:18:58.067
Jake.

00:18:58.067 --> 00:19:01.100
[ Laughter ]

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:06.334
-I guess now we know why he
calls his wife Mother, you know?

00:19:06.334 --> 00:19:07.501
-Hey!
-Okay.

00:19:07.501 --> 00:19:08.801
[ Laughter, oohs, and applause ]

00:19:08.801 --> 00:19:10.000
Don't worry.
He'll be fine,

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:11.801
once someone updates
his operating system.

00:19:11.801 --> 00:19:13.100
[ Laughter ]

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:14.968
Oh, and, throughout
the hour-long town hall,

00:19:14.968 --> 00:19:16.901
Pence seemed pretty intent
on promoting his new book.

00:19:16.901 --> 00:19:18.133
Watch this.

00:19:18.133 --> 00:19:19.534
-I appreciate you reading
my book.

00:19:19.534 --> 00:19:21.067
And I write about that
in my book.

00:19:21.067 --> 00:19:22.100
As I write in my book...

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:23.234
As I wrote in my book...

00:19:23.234 --> 00:19:24.367
And as I recount in the book...

00:19:24.367 --> 00:19:25.567
As you read in my book...

00:19:25.567 --> 00:19:27.267
I was actually there,
as I write in my book...

00:19:27.267 --> 00:19:29.200
As I write in my book...

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:30.801
And in my book...
In the back of my book...

00:19:30.801 --> 00:19:32.067
As I said at the close
of my book...

00:19:32.067 --> 00:19:33.300
I write about in my book...

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:35.501
When I sat down
to write my book...

00:19:35.501 --> 00:19:36.801
You can see the picture
in my book.

00:19:36.801 --> 00:19:39.000
Let me say,
as I said in my book...

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.901
which I appreciate you reading.

00:19:40.901 --> 00:19:41.901
[ Laughter ]
-I did.

00:19:41.901 --> 00:19:43.534
-Wow!

00:19:43.534 --> 00:19:45.467
By the end, Pence was just
answering every question like,

00:19:45.467 --> 00:19:47.033
"Well, book.
That's a very good book.

00:19:47.033 --> 00:19:48.734
I booked to that book.
You book?"

00:19:48.734 --> 00:19:50.167
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:19:50.167 --> 00:19:52.334
Some more political news.
Everyone's talking about this.

00:19:52.334 --> 00:19:54.000
More than a week
after the midterms,

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.968
Republicans finally won control
of the House.

00:19:56.968 --> 00:19:59.667
On the bright side, it's nice
to see them seizing the House

00:19:59.667 --> 00:20:01.601
without zip ties
and a Viking helmet.

00:20:01.601 --> 00:20:05.534
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:20:05.534 --> 00:20:07.834
[ Cheering ]

00:20:07.834 --> 00:20:10.300
[ Whistling ]

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:11.634
Republicans are still fighting

00:20:11.634 --> 00:20:13.934
over why they couldn't get
a few more seats.

00:20:13.934 --> 00:20:15.801
They don't know if they should
blame Trump, McConnell,

00:20:15.801 --> 00:20:16.801
or Ticketmaster.

00:20:16.801 --> 00:20:19.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:20:19.033 --> 00:20:21.033
Meanwhile, today,
Speaker Nancy Pelosi announced

00:20:21.033 --> 00:20:24.300
that she is stepping down as the
House Democratic leader.

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:29.868
Pelosi, who's 82, said it's time
for a new generation to lead.

00:20:29.868 --> 00:20:31.667
And then Biden was like,
"Whoa, whoa, whoa-kay, Nancy.

00:20:31.667 --> 00:20:34.133
Ha ha ha ha. She's funny.
Take her home. Take her home.

00:20:34.133 --> 00:20:36.701
Ha ha, she's so funny."

00:20:36.701 --> 00:20:39.534
Pelosi served as speaker
with presidents Bush, Obama,

00:20:39.534 --> 00:20:41.667
Trump, and Biden,
or, as she called them,

00:20:41.667 --> 00:20:43.467
the reason why she started
smoking, quit,

00:20:43.467 --> 00:20:45.100
then started again,
then quit again.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:20:46.133 --> 00:20:47.501
Did You guys see this?

00:20:47.501 --> 00:20:49.901
For the first time, the FDA has
approved a lab-grown meat

00:20:49.901 --> 00:20:51.367
for human consumption.

00:20:52.501 --> 00:20:54.767
The FDA was like, "Don't worry.
It's completely safe.

00:20:54.767 --> 00:20:56.501
Disgusting, but safe."
-Yeah.

00:20:57.467 --> 00:20:59.534
-Some business news --
Frontier Airline

00:20:59.534 --> 00:21:02.901
is now selling something called
the Go Wild annual pass,

00:21:02.901 --> 00:21:05.367
which offers unlimited flights
for a year.

00:21:05.367 --> 00:21:06.701
It's funny because Go Wild

00:21:06.701 --> 00:21:08.968
is also the name
of Southwest's boarding process.

00:21:08.968 --> 00:21:11.100
[ Laughter ]

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:13.801
And, finally, a new poll found
that 40% of people think

00:21:13.801 --> 00:21:16.434
Amazon has the most attractive
delivery drivers.

00:21:16.434 --> 00:21:17.901
-Ooh!
[ Laughter ]

00:21:17.901 --> 00:21:19.100
-That's why no one cares

00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:20.634
when they show up
like your package has arrived

00:21:20.634 --> 00:21:21.868
and they're not
holding anything.

00:21:23.601 --> 00:21:25.267
Guys, it's Friday.
I'm in a great mood.

00:21:25.267 --> 00:21:27.100
Unlike Twitter,
we made it to the weekend.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:30.767
You know, and I --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:21:30.767 --> 00:21:32.000
Did you see this?

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.834
After more than
1,000 key employees resigned,

00:21:34.834 --> 00:21:36.868
Twitter closed
all of their offices.

00:21:36.868 --> 00:21:38.667
And, apparently,
due to the mass resignations,

00:21:38.667 --> 00:21:41.834
the platform could start
breaking soon.

00:21:41.834 --> 00:21:46.467
Even crypto was like, "Damn.
That came crashing down fast."

00:21:47.934 --> 00:21:49.801
Right now, things are so bad,
Twitter recommends

00:21:49.801 --> 00:21:51.100
writing your tweet on
a piece of paper

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:54.267
and just mailing it to
all of your followers.

00:21:54.267 --> 00:21:56.467
Yeah, a ton of employees quit
after Elon asked them

00:21:56.467 --> 00:22:01.167
to commit to an extremely
hardcore work environment.

00:22:01.167 --> 00:22:03.434
Staff was like, "If I'm going to
go extremely hardcore

00:22:03.434 --> 00:22:04.767
for an app,
I don't want Twitter money.

00:22:04.767 --> 00:22:07.567
I want OnlyFans money."

00:22:07.567 --> 00:22:10.300
♪♪

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:11.367
-Twitter.

00:22:11.367 --> 00:22:13.367
-Last night, things got so bad,

00:22:13.367 --> 00:22:17.133
the hashtag #RIPTwitter
started trending.

00:22:17.133 --> 00:22:20.801
I just want to say, I died on
Twitter before it was cool.

00:22:20.801 --> 00:22:22.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
No big deal.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.734
♪♪

00:22:26.734 --> 00:22:28.434
Some people say
the chaos at Twitter

00:22:28.434 --> 00:22:30.968
could lead to a comeback
for Tumblr.

00:22:32.767 --> 00:22:34.234
That'd be fun to
get my political news

00:22:34.234 --> 00:22:36.567
at the same place I used to post
my Urkel fan fiction.

00:22:36.567 --> 00:22:38.501
I think that'd be fun.

00:22:38.501 --> 00:22:40.400
Yeah, Twitter's not
looking so great right now,

00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:42.701
and I think some other companies
are trying to take advantage.

00:22:42.701 --> 00:22:43.767
Check out this.
I saw this today.

00:22:43.767 --> 00:22:46.133
-Twitter is
an absolute disaster,

00:22:46.133 --> 00:22:49.534
a horrible company that's
terribly run in every way.

00:22:49.534 --> 00:22:52.901
So when thinking of us,
remember, there's worse.

00:22:55.801 --> 00:22:58.167
-I go, "Oh, now I get it. Yeah.

00:22:58.167 --> 00:22:59.667
Now I get it."

00:23:02.267 --> 00:23:03.634
Some news from Washington.

00:23:03.634 --> 00:23:05.334
Tomorrow, President Biden's
granddaughter

00:23:05.334 --> 00:23:08.267
is getting married on the
South Lawn of The White House.

00:23:08.267 --> 00:23:09.467
That's nice. It's interesting.

00:23:09.467 --> 00:23:12.601
To RSVP, you had to check
"yes" or "Ivanka."

00:23:14.868 --> 00:23:17.100
Not gonna show up, no.

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:18.367
Biden's already emotional.

00:23:18.367 --> 00:23:20.534
It's the first time an
80-year-old has ever said,

00:23:20.534 --> 00:23:22.367
"Get on my lawn.

00:23:24.734 --> 00:23:26.968
The South Lawn."

00:23:26.968 --> 00:23:28.234
It's different getting married

00:23:28.234 --> 00:23:29.434
when your grandfather's
president, though.

00:23:29.434 --> 00:23:31.167
You get cards that say,
"Enjoy the panini maker,

00:23:31.167 --> 00:23:34.067
love Kim Jong-un."

00:23:34.067 --> 00:23:36.601
Yeah, the Biden family has
a lot to celebrate this weekend,

00:23:36.601 --> 00:23:39.100
'cause on Sunday,
the president turns 80.

00:23:39.100 --> 00:23:40.601
Wow.

00:23:40.601 --> 00:23:43.667
Just to give you a sense of
how old that is, consider this.

00:23:43.667 --> 00:23:45.767
He's 80.

00:23:47.300 --> 00:23:49.033
Democrats don't want to
take any chances,

00:23:49.033 --> 00:23:52.868
so there are going to be
no surprise parties.

00:23:52.868 --> 00:23:54.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:02.000
Don't clap too loud.
He might be watching.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.334
Hey, this is big.

00:24:03.334 --> 00:24:04.567
Today, the Justice Department

00:24:04.567 --> 00:24:06.634
named a special counsel
to investigate whether

00:24:06.634 --> 00:24:09.901
former president Trump should be
charged for January 6th

00:24:09.901 --> 00:24:12.000
or taking classified documents.

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:15.000
As we speak, Trump is squeezing
into a turkey costume

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:17.234
to trick Biden
into pardoning him.

00:24:20.801 --> 00:24:22.601
[ As Trump ] Gobble, gobble.

00:24:23.901 --> 00:24:26.434
Gobble, gobble.

00:24:27.634 --> 00:24:29.767
[ Normal voice ] Switching
gears. Some big sports news.

00:24:29.767 --> 00:24:32.267
This weekend,
the World Cup begins in Qatar.

00:24:32.267 --> 00:24:35.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:38.067
Yep. Soccer is huge
across the world.

00:24:38.067 --> 00:24:39.501
Meanwhile,
Americans are like, "Wait.

00:24:39.501 --> 00:24:42.367
'Ted Lasso'
is based on a real sport?"

00:24:43.033 --> 00:24:45.801
Disney, I saw
that they just filed a patent

00:24:45.801 --> 00:24:46.934
for a new type of
roller coaster,

00:24:46.934 --> 00:24:48.067
and it looks pretty crazy.

00:24:48.067 --> 00:24:49.100
Watch this.

00:24:49.100 --> 00:24:51.667
-Walt Disney just filed a patent

00:24:51.667 --> 00:24:54.300
for a roller coaster
that jumps the track?

00:24:54.300 --> 00:24:56.267
Engineers say it has to move

00:24:56.267 --> 00:24:58.434
at precise speed
every single time,

00:24:58.434 --> 00:25:01.434
which can easily be impacted by
the weather, by humidity,

00:25:01.434 --> 00:25:04.567
number of riders,
and many, many other elements.

00:25:04.567 --> 00:25:08.100
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:10.968
-The ride is called You First.

00:25:10.968 --> 00:25:13.167
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:25:13.167 --> 00:25:14.601
Don't worry -- they're going to
put some pillows

00:25:14.601 --> 00:25:17.000
down the first few times they
try it, so it should be alright.

00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:18.501
It's the only ride
with a sign that says,

00:25:18.501 --> 00:25:20.534
"You must be this tall to die."

00:25:20.534 --> 00:25:21.601
But this is nice.

00:25:21.601 --> 00:25:23.000
Disney takes your picture
during the ride,

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:27.133
and a crime-scene photographer
takes it after.

00:25:27.133 --> 00:25:29.334
"Jumps the tracks."

00:25:29.334 --> 00:25:30.901
Meanwhile,
Six Flags was like, "Big deal.

00:25:30.901 --> 00:25:33.000
We've been doing that
for years."

00:25:35.300 --> 00:25:37.267
Get this -- the makers of
Scrabble have announced

00:25:37.267 --> 00:25:39.334
that they now will accept
hundreds of new words.

00:25:39.334 --> 00:25:40.567
-Oh!

00:25:40.567 --> 00:25:42.334
-Check out this commercial they
just released.

00:25:42.334 --> 00:25:45.834
-America's most beloved
board game is better than ever,

00:25:45.834 --> 00:25:48.167
with hundreds of
new playable words, like...

00:25:50.868 --> 00:25:54.634
And to make it even more fun,
we now accept misspelled words,

00:25:54.634 --> 00:25:57.634
made-up words, and tater tots.

00:26:01.067 --> 00:26:02.701
-Interesting, right?
-Wow!

00:26:04.334 --> 00:26:06.801
Wow! Indeed.

00:26:06.801 --> 00:26:11.400
-Also, I read that Tyson Foods
recalled 94,000 pounds

00:26:11.400 --> 00:26:13.334
of ground beef
'cause it may contain

00:26:13.334 --> 00:26:16.033
a hard, mirror-like substance.

00:26:16.033 --> 00:26:19.467
They're really bending over
backwards to avoid saying,

00:26:19.467 --> 00:26:22.000
"Fine, it's glass, okay?"

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:24.634
A "mirror-like substance"?

00:26:24.634 --> 00:26:26.434
Nothing worse than eating
a 1-pound burger

00:26:26.434 --> 00:26:28.367
and catching
a glimpse of yourself.

00:26:28.367 --> 00:26:30.133
"Ugh! That's what I look like?"

